# The build context is sent to the daemon before the build starts, so everything
# excluded here is both a smaller upload and a smaller surface for an accidental
# `COPY .`.

# Configuration. `.env` holds real credentials on this machine; the image reads
# its configuration from the environment instead, so this is excluded first among
# equals. The example file has no values to leak.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies and build output are produced inside the image. A local
# `node_modules` or `dist` would be platform-specific and would shadow what the
# build stage just compiled.
node_modules
dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test output, not test sources: `tests/` is copied into the build stage because
# `tsc --noEmit` typechecks it.
coverage

# Version control and CI metadata are not build inputs, and `.git` alone is
# usually the largest thing in a context.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local tooling and editor cruft.
.husky
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log
pnpm-debug.log*
